 "role": "Verification: per-session data-quality report (point count, duration, max gap, RR drift, artifact %, ectopy %, out-of-range %) producing pass/fail (RR drift only ever warns), rejection reasons, localized errors/warnings and metrics. A report, not a gate: analysis runs regardless; the result is stored on SessionState.verificationResult for the record view's badge and its summary goes to the diagnostic log.",
 "types": [
  "Verification: struct — verifier with Config",
  "Verification.RejectionReason: enum String Codable — seven cases; the checks produce six of them (excessiveDrift is no longer produced and is kept so stored results still decode)",
  "Verification.Result: struct Codable",
  "Verification.Metrics: struct Codable",
  "Verification.Config: struct — thresholds (default, strict)",
  "Verification.SeriesStats: struct — precomputed stats"
 ],
 "state": [
  "mem:Verification.Config.default",
  "mem:Verification.Config.strict"
 ],
 "toplevel": "Config.default (minPoints 300, 0.083 h, max artifact 15%, warn 5%) and Config.strict (4 h). RRCollector.swift builds a relaxed streaming config (120 pts, 0.025 h, 20%/10%). The stored `config` is internal (read-only), so the Record tab's Data Quality card can judge a result by the limits of the verifier that produced it (RecordView.verificationLimits).",
